  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 2.00 ERP line for gantry 'CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)' on TRP-00521 was charged for a line the GPS trace never crossed, so it is a phantom charge. It has been refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction; review the ERP selection on this trip (the driver's statement records a possible mistaken selection) as a billing-integrity matter."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the whole of the SGD 2.00 you contested is returned to you, and both advocates agree it should be. This was an upfront-quoted trip (fare_breakdown.fare_model = UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd = SGD 10.00) on which you were charged charged_total = SGD 12.00. The entire SGD 2.00 difference is a single ERP line (fare_breakdown.tolls_erp = SGD 2.00) for the gantry 'CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)'. That line does not stand: the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00521) is complete and clean — 73 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0 — and its closest approach to the gantry is 6,778 m, roughly twenty-seven times the 250 m POL-RD-09(4) crossing radius, with gap_brackets_closest_approach false. The ledger itself marks the line 'crossed': false and on_optimal_route = false, splitting on_optimal_route_total 0.00 against off_optimal_route_total 2.00. Under POL-RD-09(4) a gantry charge the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction available whether or not a deviation exists, and POL-RD-10(8) is expressly not triggered by a line refunded under that limb. The same result follows under POL-RD-11(a): your remedy is charged_total less quoted_fare_sgd less the pass-through lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09; properly_chargeable.total is SGD 0.00 (erp_total 0.00, airport_surcharge 0.00, waiting_time_fee 0.00), so the amount is SGD 12.00 − SGD 10.00 = SGD 2.00, equal to the published pol_rd_11_remedy of 2.00. Because the whole contested sum is returned, the outcome is FULL_REFUND. No distance remedy is added on top and none is double-counted: POL-RD-11(a) and POL-RD-09(4) are the same SGD 2.00, stated once.\n\nOn the routing question, nothing is owed either way. The measured excess is 0.18 km, or 4.6% of the 3.9 km optimal (trace_distance_km 4.08 against optimal_distance_km 3.9), below both POL-RD-01 thresholds of 0.8 km and 20%, so no deviation is established and the outcome is not one 'however the rider characterises the trip'. In any event this is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip, so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: no distance-or-time refund is available regardless of the excess. The two advocates' characterisations of the SGD 2.00 — billing correction (driver) versus full refund of the contested amount (rider) — come to the same figure, and that figure is awarded.\n\nTo the driver: your own account on the file — that the meter adds ERP automatically when you select it and that you 'might have pressed it by mistake' — is an admission against your own interest and is consistent with the trace, which places the vehicle nowhere near the CTE corridor at the 21:47:40 charge time. Nothing in the trip record or the 73 fixes supports the line. This is not a finding about your routing on this trip: no deviation was committed, and no POL-RD-06 driver-profile uplift or conduct referral arises, because POL-RD-06 requires a MATERIAL deviation and there is none. No driver compensation is due: you were billed 4.1 km against a 4.08 km trace, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall.\n\nCredibility and confidence: the finding rests on EV-FARE-00521 and EV-GPS-00521, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap on confidence is 1.0 and the ruling sits at 0.95. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00521-01 (status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0) carries no fact and the ruling does not rely on it; its absence is noted and is not an escalation trigger, because no exculpatory traffic clause was invoked against it — no party asserted an external traffic cause for any measured deviation, so POL-RD-03 and POL-RD-13 are not in play and POL-RD-10(5) does not fire. The GPS trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), trip identifier TRP-00521 matches across the trip record, trace and ledger, the timestamps run forward and agree, and the only unmatched charge line is the ERP line refunded under POL-RD-09(4) — so no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires and a monetary ruling issues."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

