    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the disputed sum is the SGD 2.00 'ERP' line on a SGD 12.00 card charge against a SGD 10.00 upfront quote. I rule a FULL_REFUND of SGD 2.00 to the rider, with a billing-integrity referral that does not delay the money.\n\nWhy the whole SGD 2.00 comes back. This was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: the fare was fixed at booking at SGD 10.00 (fare_breakdown.quoted_fare_sgd = 10.00) and the card was charged SGD 12.00 (fare_breakdown.charged_total = 12.00). The entire difference is the single ERP line of SGD 2.00 (fare_breakdown.tolls_erp = 2.00). Under POL-RD-11(a) the rider recovers the amount by which the charge exceeds the quote, less only those pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. This line is not properly chargeable. The only gantry charged is 'CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)'; it is not on the booked optimal route (fare_breakdown.erp_gantries on_optimal_route = false, off_optimal_route_total 2.00 against on_optimal_route_total 0.00), and the vehicle never passed it — the closest of the trace's 73 fixes is 6,778.01 m away against the POL-RD-09(4) 250 m crossing radius, and gap_brackets_closest_approach is false. The ledger reaches the same conclusion: properly_chargeable.total is SGD 0.00 and its own pol_rd_11_remedy is SGD 2.00. That makes this a phantom gantry line, refundable in full as a standalone billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4), available whether or not a deviation exists. 12.00 − 10.00 − 0.00 = 2.00, already a multiple of SGD 0.05.\n\nOn the routing itself there is no deviation, and nothing in this ruling rests on the driver having taken a wrong route. The trace records 4.08 km against a 3.9 km optimal — an excess of 0.18 km, or 4.6% — below both POL-RD-01 thresholds (0.8 km and 20%). I therefore accept the driver's POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-08 points that no deviation is established and the burden never shifts, and that on an upfront trip no distance-or-time refund arises (POL-RD-11). That does not change the outcome: the rider's entitlement is a charge-correction available independently of any deviation under POL-RD-09(4), and the driver's own advocate concedes the SGD 2.00 correction.\n\nThe driver's account — that the meter adds ERP automatically when selected and that he 'might have pressed it by mistake' — is evidence on the file, and it agrees with the trace and the ledger. No external traffic cause is asserted by anyone, so the bundle's traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00521-01, which is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0), carries no fact here and nothing rests on it.\n\nOn escalation: the trace is COMPLETE and unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c) (73 fixes, 10 s cadence, max_gap_sec 0.0, no jumps), trip identifier TRP-00521 matches across all three instruments, timestamps run forward and agree, and the single unmatched charge line is one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-09(4) and POL-RD-10(8) expressly exclude from the unmatched-line trigger. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires, so the case is decided rather than escalated. No POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral applies, because there is no material deviation on this trip.\n\nConfidence rests on EV-GPS-00521, EV-FARE-00521 and EV-TRIP-00521, all at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

