    "explanation": "Both sides actually agree on the substance, and the record confirms it, so this is decided on the fare ledger and the trace and not on the routing question.\n\nWhat was charged. This was an upfront-quoted trip (fare_breakdown.fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE). The fare was fixed at SGD 10.00 (quoted_fare_sgd) and SGD 12.00 was taken from the card (charged_total). The entire SGD 2.00 difference is one ERP line for the gantry 'CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)' (fare_breakdown.tolls_erp 2.00; erp_lines amount 2.00).\n\nWhy that line cannot stand. POL-RD-09(4) matches a gantry to the GPS trace by treating any fix within 250 m of the gantry as a crossing. The nearest of the trace's 73 fixes (EV-GPS-00521, COMPLETE, weight 1.0) is 6,778.01 m from the gantry — roughly twenty-seven times the crossing radius — and gap_brackets_closest_approach is false. The vehicle never went near the gantry. The ledger's own derived block says the same: crossed = false, on_optimal_route = false, erp_total 0.00 after excluding the uncrossed line. A charge line for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4): it is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. The driver's own statement that the meter adds ERP when he selects it and that he 'might have pressed it by mistake' is an admission against his interest and is entirely consistent with the trace; it is treated as evidence of the thing conceded.\n\nThe deviation question both advocates raise. The trace shows an excess of only 0.18 km, or 4.6%, over the 3.9 km optimal route, below both POL-RD-01 thresholds (0.8 km and 20%), so no route deviation is established and the driver's burden under POL-RD-08 never arises. That is correct, and it is also irrelevant to the refund: POL-RD-09(4) makes the phantom-line correction available whether or not a deviation exists, and on an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-11 bars any distance-or-time refund in any event. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00521-01, MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed by the rider's own claim and cannot rescue the line — no advisory is on file, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and no external-cause excuse carries weight; but nothing turns on it here, because the refund rests on the uncrossed gantry, not on the routing.\n\nThe amount, read off the record. charged_total 12.00 less quoted_fare 10.00 = 2.00; properly_chargeable.total is 0.00 (erp_total 0.00 once the uncrossed line is excluded, airport_surcharge 0.00, waiting_time_fee 0.00); the ledger publishes pol_rd_11_remedy 2.00 with pol_rd_11_remedy_available true. The full SGD 2.00 you paid over the quote is returned to you, the rider.\n\nRuling. The whole contested sum is returned, so this is a FULL_REFUND of SGD 2.00 to the rider. The refund is a pass-through correction, not a finding against the driver's routing on this trip, so no driver compensation is due and none is awarded. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires (identifiers match, timestamps run forward, the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c), POL-RD-02 does not run on an upfront fare, and the only unmatched line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excludes), so this is decided rather than escalated. Confidence rests on a clean trace at weight 1.0 and the fare ledger at weight 1.0; the cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0 and no down-weighted artifact carries the finding."
