oduces the POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral above.\n\nThe bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00521-01, is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0, no payload). No advisory covers the corridor, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and no external-cause excuse carries weight (POL-RD-13). That absence decides nothing here: neither party advanced a traffic excuse, and the deviation claim fails on its own threshold regardless. The missing artifact carries no fact and does not enter the confidence.\n\nNo POL-RD-10 trigger fires. Trip identifiers match (TRP-00521 across trip record, trace and ledger); timestamps run forward and agree; the trace is clean under POL-RD-07(a)–(c) (73 fixes, 10 s cadence, zero gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0); and the only unmatched charge line is the ERP line itself, which POL-RD-09(4) expressly excludes from the POL-RD-10(8) trigger. POL-RD-06 is not engaged because no material deviation exists, so no driver-conduct referral is due and no POL-RD-06(b) uplift applies. No driver compensation arises either: the charged distance (4.1 km) is not less than the trace distance (4.08 km), so the POL-RD-04 unbilled-distance shortfall test is not met.\n\nConfidence: the deciding fact — that the gantry was never crossed — is carried by EV-GPS-00521 and EV-FARE-00521, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. I set confidence at 0.95. The rider_profile carries no corroboration burden (deviation_claims_60d 0, deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0, far below the POL-RD-08 threshold), and no context-only profile field has been used as a ground of decision by either side."
